Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/kgsl: never shadow a resource imported from a dma-buf

Base: lfdevs/mesa-for-android-container 98f3d6229d61452cef80f8563af7c56ae599dc14

With FD_KGSL_ENABLE_DMABUF, fd_resource_get_handle() shadowed every resource
not created with PIPE_BIND_SHARED: it copied the contents into new storage
once and swapped the resource onto that copy. A resource imported from a
dma-buf is not created with that bind, and GBM queries the KMS handle of
every buffer it imports (gbm_dri_bo_import, dri2_query_image ->
resource_get_handle). So each buffer imported through GBM, as glamor imports
every DRI3 pixmap, kept the contents it had at import, and no later write by
the client reached the X server. Import through EGL_LINUX_DMA_BUF_EXT, which
queries no handle, was unaffected.

Evidence: M19 R4m, docs/m19-r4m-result.md. The same buffer, written after
import, read 0 of 1000 through GBM and 1000 through EGL in one process.
The fork made the same change in 84fc50fab2 (2026-10-08), among others.

---
diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_resource.c b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_resource.c
index bcb6c2c..7781f26 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_resource.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_resource.c
@@ -1098,6 +1098,10 @@ fd_resource_get_handle(struct pipe_screen *pscreen, struct pipe_context *pctx,
    assert_dt
 {
    struct fd_resource *rsc = fd_resource(prsc);
+   /* resource_from_handle() marks an imported resource shared.  Sample it
+    * before this function does: a handle query on an imported resource must
+    * never replace its storage. */
+   const bool imported = rsc->b.is_shared;
 
    rsc->b.is_shared = true;
 
@@ -1110,16 +1114,23 @@ fd_resource_get_handle(struct pipe_screen *pscreen, struct pipe_context *pctx,
       handle->modifier = DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR;
 
       if (!(prsc->bind & PIPE_BIND_SHARED)) {
-         struct fd_context *ctx = fd_screen_aux_context_get(pscreen);
-
          prsc->bind |= PIPE_BIND_SHARED;
 
-         bool ret = fd_try_shadow_resource(ctx, rsc, 0, NULL, handle->modifier);
+         /* Shadowing copies the contents into new storage once.  For a
+          * resource imported from another process's dma-buf, every later
+          * write by that process would then be lost: GBM queries the handle
+          * of every buffer it imports, so glamor would keep each DRI3 buffer
+          * as it was at import. */
+         if (!imported) {
+            struct fd_context *ctx = fd_screen_aux_context_get(pscreen);
+
+            bool ret = fd_try_shadow_resource(ctx, rsc, 0, NULL, handle->modifier);
 
-         fd_screen_aux_context_put(pscreen);
+            fd_screen_aux_context_put(pscreen);
 
-         if (!ret)
-            return false;
+            if (!ret)
+               return false;
+         }
       }
    }
 
